James inquired about deploying a Shiny app with data files located in subfolders. I provided a step-by-step guide detailing how to ensure these files are included during deployment, specifically using `rsconnect::deployApp()`. James indicated the issue with missing files not specified in his `appFiles` list. I advised on explicitly including necessary files, utilizing wildcards in `list.files()` for easier file management, and using the `pattern` argument for filtering. We explored examples of listing all files or specific file types in a directory, culminating in a recommended deployment approach that ensures all relevant data files are bundled with the app.
